    <requiresclause>std::invocable&lt;Callable_T&amp;&gt;    </requiresclause>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Checks whether a callable throws a specific exception, for <computeroutput>expect()</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>require()</computeroutput>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The callable is invoked once, immediately. The check passes if it throws an exception of type <computeroutput>Exception_T</computeroutput> or of a type derived from it, so <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-exceptions_1ga6a0ca4f8b757ea511c494189212812b3" kindref="member">throws</ref>&lt;std::exception&gt;()</computeroutput> passes for any standard exception. An exception of another type, or no exception, fails the check, and the report states what was thrown.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Exception_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the exception expected to be thrown. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Callable_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type of the callable object to be invoked; it must be invocable without arguments, as an lvalue, so a <computeroutput>mutable</computeroutput> lambda is accepted. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>func</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The callable object to check for exception throwing behaviour. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>An object of an unspecified type, holding the result, to be passed to <computeroutput>expect()</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>require()</computeroutput>.</para>
</simplesect>
The <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-exceptions_1ga6a0ca4f8b757ea511c494189212812b3" kindref="member">throws</ref></computeroutput> function template verifies whether invoking the provided callable object results in the throwing of a specific exception type within the µTest++ framework. This is useful for testing error handling in code under test. Exceptions of other types are reported as failures.</para>
<para>The callable is invoked immediately, when the comparator is constructed; the result is reported when the comparator is passed to <computeroutput>expect()</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>require()</computeroutput>, which also accept optional messages. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
