      </memberdef>
    </sectiondef>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Functions for verifying exceptions in test cases. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Three functions check what a callable throws, and are used as the conditions of <computeroutput>expect()</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>require()</computeroutput>:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>mt::throws (callable)</computeroutput> is true when the callable throws any exception;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>mt::throws&lt;E&gt; (callable)</computeroutput> is true when it throws an exception of type <computeroutput>E</computeroutput>, or of a type derived from it;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>mt::nothrow (callable)</computeroutput> is true when it throws nothing.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>The exception is caught by the check, so it does not leave the test case. When the check fails, the report states why, for example:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>throws&lt;std::runtime_error&gt;, but nothing was thrown</computeroutput>;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>throws&lt;std::runtime_error&gt;, but a std::exception was thrown: "what"</computeroutput>, with the text returned by its <computeroutput>what()</computeroutput>;</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>nothrow, but an exception of unknown type was thrown</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>A failed <computeroutput>require()</computeroutput> inside the callable is not an exception of the callable: it stops the test case, as it does elsewhere, and does not satisfy <computeroutput>throws()</computeroutput> or fail <computeroutput>nothrow()</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Example</title><para></para>
</simplesect>
<programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="normal">ts.test<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;Check<sp/>if<sp/>exceptions<sp/>are<sp/>thrown&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>[]<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal">&amp;<sp/>t)<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(mt::throws<sp/>([]<sp/>{<sp/>exercise_throw<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">true</highlight><highlight class="normal">);<sp/>}))</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;exception<sp/>thrown&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(mt::throws&lt;std::runtime_error&gt;<sp/>([]</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>{<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">throw</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>std::runtime_error{<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>};<sp/>}))</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;std::runtime_error<sp/>thrown&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(mt::nothrow<sp/>([]<sp/>{<sp/>exercise_throw<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">false</highlight><highlight class="normal">);<sp/>}))</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;exception<sp/>not<sp/>thrown&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">});</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Availability</title><para>The functions are declared only when the compiler defines <computeroutput>__cpp_exceptions</computeroutput>. In a build without exceptions (for example with <computeroutput>-fno-exceptions</computeroutput>), the code under test cannot throw, the functions do not exist, and a test case that calls them does not compile; guard such test cases with <computeroutput>#if defined(__cpp_exceptions)</computeroutput>.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Several exception types</title><para>To accept one of several exception types, use a <computeroutput>try</computeroutput> block with a <computeroutput>catch</computeroutput> for each type, and report each outcome with <computeroutput>expect (true)</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>expect (false)</computeroutput>. Check the normal path too, after the call in the <computeroutput>try</computeroutput> block; otherwise a call that throws nothing passes with no check:</para>
</simplesect>
<programlisting filename=".cpp"><codeline><highlight class="normal">ts.test<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;Check<sp/>exceptions<sp/>explicitly&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">,<sp/>[]<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal">&amp;<sp/>t)<sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">try</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>compute_answer<sp/>();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">false</highlight><highlight class="normal">)<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;no<sp/>exception<sp/>thrown&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">catch</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">const</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>std::overflow_error&amp;<sp/>e)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">true</highlight><highlight class="normal">)<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;std::overflow_error<sp/>thrown&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">catch</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">const</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>std::runtime_error&amp;<sp/>e)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">true</highlight><highlight class="normal">)<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;std::runtime_error<sp/>thrown&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">catch</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>(...)</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>{</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>t.expect<sp/>(</highlight><highlight class="keyword">false</highlight><highlight class="normal">)<sp/>&lt;&lt;<sp/></highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;unknown<sp/>exception<sp/>thrown&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><sp/><sp/><sp/><sp/>}</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">});</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting>  </para>
    </detaileddescription>
  </compounddef>
